304
00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:48.700
Spurring on a deep dive.
激发你深入探究的兴趣。

305
00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:49.500
Yes.
是的。

306
00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:56.800
And, you know, the thing is, is that making the podcast is that same touchstone for me.
你知道吗，对我来说，制作播客也是同样的慰藉。

307
00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:04.240
Coming in here each week and making this podcast, whatever else is going on in my life, all of
每周来到这里制作这档播客，无论我的生活中发生了什么，无论那些

308
00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:07.300
the things, because we all always have all of the things, you know?
琐事，因为我们每个人总是有处理不完的琐事，你懂的吧？

309
00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.100
Yes, everybody is carrying so much.
没错，每个人都背负着沉重的压力。

310
00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:09.460
Yeah.
是啊。

311
00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.700
And we don't know what everybody is carrying.
我们并不知道每个人都在承受着什么。

312
00:14:12.060 --> 00:14:12.160
That's right.
说得对。

313
00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.780
But everyone's got something, right?
但每个人都有自己的难处，对吧？

314
00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:22.520
And this is that same escape and release and laughter and fun for me, making it, that it
对我而言，制作这档节目就像是同样的逃避、释放、欢笑和乐趣，听起来

315
00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.820
sounds like it is for Jacqueline when she listens.
就像杰奎琳在收听时感受到的那样。

316
00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:26.120
And it makes me so happy.
这让我感到非常开心。

317
00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:26.820
Me too.
我也是。

318
00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.620
It made me so happy to read that letter.
读到那封信让我感到非常高兴。

319
00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:31.080
Jacqueline, thank you for taking the time to write us.
杰奎琳，谢谢你抽出时间写信给我们。

320
00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:33.640
And like Jenna said, we're here for you.
就像珍娜说的，我们一直在这里支持你。

321
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:36.760
Well, I think that is a nice time to take a break.
好吧，我觉得现在是休息一下的好时机。

322
00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:40.120
Yes, because when we come back, we're going to catch up with Andy.
没错，因为回来之后，我们要去看看安迪的情况。

323
00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:41.660
He's on his boat.
他在他的船上。

324
00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:42.780
It's not going well.
情况不太妙。

325
00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:43.880
No, it is not.
确实不太妙。

326
00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:57.320
We are back on Andy's boat.
我们回到了安迪的船上。

327
00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:01.180
And he's, I guess, doing some form of FaceTime.
我想他正在用某种形式进行FaceTime通话。

328
00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:02.560
I think he's Skyping.
我觉得他在用Skype。

329
00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:03.080
Skype.
Skype。

330
00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.060
Yes, Skype.
是的，Skype。

331
00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:04.880
They said Skype?
他们说是Skype吗？

332
00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:06.200
Of course, I would get that wrong.
我当然会搞错。

333
00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:07.460
I'm going to get all of that wrong.
我肯定会把这些都搞错的。

334
00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:08.800
Do people still Skype?
现在还有人用Skype吗？

335
00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.180
I don't know.
我不知道。

336
00:15:10.560 --> 00:15:11.620
Now we Zoom, right?
现在我们都用Zoom了，对吧？

337
00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:12.420
Now we Zoom.
现在我们用Zoom。

338
00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.460
We Skyped, then we FaceTimed, now we Zoom.
我们用过Skype，然后是FaceTime，现在是Zoom。

339
00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:18.220
I still FaceTime with my mom, but she calls it Facebook.
我还会和我妈FaceTime，但她管这叫Facebook。

340
00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:19.660
So she'll say, do you want a Facebook?
所以她会问，你想来个Facebook吗？

341
00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:21.340
And I'm like, I FaceTime.
我就说，我是在FaceTime。

342
00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:21.880
Yeah.
是啊。

343
00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.580
But I am becoming my mom.
但我正在变得越来越像我妈。

344
00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.040
You are, slowly.
你确实在慢慢变像她。

345
00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:25.500
Slowly.
慢慢地。

346
00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:33.880
He shares with everyone that he's been watching Dirty Dancing on repeat, and he's super sunburned because Walter Jr.
他告诉大家他一直在循环播放《辣身舞》，而且他晒伤得很严重，因为小沃尔特

347
00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:35.780
has been hoarding all the sunscreen.
把防晒霜都囤起来了。

348
00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:41.960
Yeah, while he's talking with everyone, he manages to drop his drinking water overboard.
是啊，在和大家聊天的时候，他竟然把饮用水掉进了海里。

349
00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.860
Then he drops his desalinator overboard.
然后他又把海水淡化器掉进了海里。

350
00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.060
And you know what?
你知道吗？

351
00:15:46.100 --> 00:15:46.880
He looks awful.
他看起来糟透了。

352
00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.540
He looks like he's going crazy.
他看起来快疯了。

353
00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:49.480
I know.
我知道。

354
00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:50.240
He does.
确实如此。

355
00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:51.400
Daryl says, you know what?
达里尔说，你知道吗？

356
00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:53.000
He's only been sailing for two days.
他才出海两天而已。

357
00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:53.420
Yeah.
是啊。

358
00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:56.780
I mean, he looks like he's been out to sea for months.
我的意思是，他看起来像是在海上漂了几个月一样。

359
00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:59.840
There were some alts within this scene.
这场戏里有一些备选台词。

360
00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:05.400
You know when Andy says, be more worried about my eyes because they've become flaming meatballs in my skull?
记得安迪说的那句吗，比起我的眼睛，你更该担心，因为它们在我的眼眶里已经变成了燃烧的肉丸？

361
00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:07.280
Here was his alt.
这是他的备选台词。

362
00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:10.760
If you want to worry about some part of my body, worry about my eyes.
如果你非要担心我身体的某个部位，那就担心我的眼睛吧。

363
00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:13.380
Brush my teeth with a sea urchin this AM.
今天早上我用海胆刷了牙。

364
00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:14.440
Oh, boy.
天哪。

365
00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:14.980
I know.
我知道。

366
00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:19.120
I think the writers had a lot of fun pitching this Andy Boat stuff.
我觉得编剧们在构思安迪出海这段情节时一定玩得很开心。

367
00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:22.880
One of the other lines was he said, my skin's too sensitive now.
其中还有一句台词是他说，我的皮肤现在太敏感了。

368
00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:25.400
The shirt part of my life is over, dudes.
我的人生从此告别衬衫了，伙计们。

369
00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:27.140
He's not going to wear shirts anymore.
他以后再也不穿衬衫了。

370
00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:27.500
No.
没错。

371
00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:27.860
That's it.
就是这样。

372
00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:28.580
He's done with shirts.
他彻底不穿衬衫了。

373
00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:30.660
He has no sunscreen, but he's going to take off his shirt.
他没有防晒霜，却要把衬衫脱掉。

374
00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:31.780
That's a great idea.
真是个好主意。

375
00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:32.380
Yeah, I know.
是啊，我知道。

376
00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:34.400
We had a fan question from Olivia B.
我们收到了一位来自拉斯维加斯的粉丝奥利维亚·B的提问，

377
00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:36.520
in Las Vegas who really loved the line,
她非常喜欢那句台词，

378
00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:38.440
keeps my hair out of my stare.
让我的头发不挡住我的视线。

379
00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:39.420
I loved that.
我超爱那句。

380
00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:41.200
Also helps me combat the glare bear.
还能帮我对抗那只炫目熊。

381
00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:43.360
I loved that line too, Olivia.
我也很喜欢那句台词，奥利维亚。

382
00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:46.000
Olivia wanted to know who wrote that line.
奥利维亚想知道是谁写了那句台词。

383
00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:47.280
Oh, I have a guess.
哦，我有个猜测。

384
00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:48.100
Did you find out?
你查到了吗？

385
00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:48.640
I did.
查到了。

386
00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:49.620
Carrie told me.
嘉莉告诉我的。

387
00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:50.480
Was it Brent?
是布伦特写的吗？

388
00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:54.960
It was not, but that is such a good guess because he loves the puns.
不是，但你猜得真准，因为他特别喜欢双关语。

389
00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:55.380
I know.
我知道。

390
00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:55.780
Who was it?
那是谁写的？

391
00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:56.640
Although that's not a pun.
虽然那不算双关语。

392
00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:57.720
It's more of a rhyme, right?
那更像是个押韵，对吧？

393
00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:59.500
I know, but still very Brent-ish.
我知道，但还是很像布伦特的风格。

394
00:16:59.740 --> 00:16:59.920
Very Brent.
非常有布伦特的味道。

395
00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:00.320
Okay.
好吧。

396
00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:04.420
Carrie said, Olivia, I am so happy you asked this question.
嘉莉说，奥利维亚，我很高兴你问了这个问题。

397
00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:07.260
It was written by our writer, Graham Wagner.
那是我们的编剧格雷厄姆·瓦格纳写的。

398
00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.100
She said, Graham is a good friend.
她说，格雷厄姆是个好朋友。

399
00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:11.140
They went on to write on Silicon Valley together.
他们后来还一起参与了《硅谷》的编剧工作。

400
00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:17.740
And she said she completely remembers cracking up in Paul Lieberstein's office when Graham pitched
她说她完全记得当时在保罗·利伯斯坦的办公室里，听到格雷厄姆提出这个点子时，大家都笑翻了。

401
00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:18.380
that line.
那句台词。

402
00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:19.900
I love that.
我喜欢那句。

403
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.680
So she's so glad you appreciated it.
所以她很高兴你能欣赏它。

404
00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.300
Well, Graham, way to go.
好吧，格雷厄姆，干得好。

405
00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:29.440
So as Andy's dropping everything that's important over the side of the boat, including his laptop,
当安迪把所有重要的东西都扔到船外时，包括他的笔记本电脑，

406
00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:31.380
I wrote two words.
我写了两个词。

407
00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:32.160
What?
什么？

408
00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:33.400
Fumble fingers.
笨手笨脚。

409
00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:34.020
Oh.
哦。

410
00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:35.340
Because.
因为。

411
00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:37.060
He has a real fumble fingers.
他真是个笨手笨脚的人。

412
00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:41.140
This is the thing my dad used to say when we were like teenagers clomping through the
这是我爸爸以前常说的话，那时我们还是青少年，在屋里走得重重地，

413
00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:42.340
house and we would drop things.
还会弄掉东西。

414
00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:45.820
My dad would be like, someone's got a case of the fumble fingers.
我爸爸会说，有人又笨手笨脚了。

415
00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:49.040
Well, I'll have you know, we really shot that on a boat.
好吧，我得让你知道，我们真的是在船上拍的。

416
00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:56.320
We shot Andy's side of the conversation the week prior when we were shooting the boat and
我们在拍摄船上戏份的前一周拍了安迪那边的对话，

417
00:17:56.320 --> 00:18:00.940
getting that shot of the laptop going into the water was a really time consuming shot.
拍笔记本电脑掉进水里的那个镜头非常耗时。

418
00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:01.660
I bet.
我敢打赌。

419
00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:07.960
So what they did was our cinematographer put a waterproof GoPro camera and he attached it
所以他们做的是，我们的摄影师装了一个防水的GoPro摄像机，把它绑在

420
00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:12.660
to a stick because they had to make sure that the camera didn't really sink.
一根棍子上，因为他们必须确保摄像机不会真的沉下去。

421
00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:13.240
Right.
没错。

422
00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:16.040
But they also had to make sure it looked realistic.
但他们也必须确保它看起来很真实。

423
00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:23.660
So it was like many times of someone like using this GoPro on a stick to look like fall
所以就像有人多次用这根绑着GoPro的棍子来模拟坠落，

424
00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:26.280
and then bobbing and all that sort of stuff.
还有漂浮之类的动作。

425
00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:29.440
Also during the scene, we had a real boat captain.
在那个场景中，我们还有一位真正的船长。

426
00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:35.020
His name was Chris Roberson and he was laying on the bottom of the cockpit driving the boat.
他叫克里斯·罗伯森，他躺在驾驶舱底部开船。

427
00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:35.880
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

428
00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:37.420
The whole time we did this shot.
我们拍这个镜头的时候他一直都在。

429
00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:38.520
He was like hidden.
他就像被藏起来了一样。

430
00:18:38.920 --> 00:18:39.740
But yeah.
但确实是这样。

431
00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:44.380
You know, the very last moment where Andy says he strikes a pose and is like,
你知道，在最后一刻安迪摆了个姿势，说，

432
00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:47.000
let this be the lasting memory of a man on a boat.
让这成为一个男人在船上的永恒记忆吧。

433
00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:47.340
You know?
你知道吗？

434
00:18:47.580 --> 00:18:50.540
I have a background catch at one minute, 27 seconds.
我在一分二十七秒处发现了一个背景穿帮。

435
00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:51.140
What's that?
那是什么？

436
00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:57.220
Pam, Daryl, Angela, Phyllis, Oscar, and Aaron are all watching Andy as he drops his computer
帕姆、达里尔、安吉拉、菲利斯、奥斯卡和亚伦都在看着安迪把他的电脑

437
00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:57.900
into the water.
扔进水里。

438
00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:03.820
You even hear us react like, oh, and then at one minute, 36 seconds, we're all gone.
你甚至能听到我们的反应，比如“哦”，然后在一分三十六秒时，我们都不见了。

439
00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:05.660
Only Aaron and Daryl remain.
只剩下亚伦和达里尔。

440
00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:06.840
We left immediately.
我们立刻就离开了。

441
00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:07.560
Immediately.
立刻。

442
00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:08.700
Ran out of there.
从那里跑了出去。

443
00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:11.880
I remember shooting that that morning, Angela.
安吉拉，我记得那天早上拍那个镜头的情景。

444
00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:14.380
You know, we were not really live with him.
你知道，我们当时并没有真的和他在一起。

445
00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:14.880
No.
没有。

446
00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:20.840
But they did bring it up on the computer and I remember being like legitimately shocked
但他们确实在电脑上展示了，我记得当我看到他那层脱皮的化妆效果时，

447
00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.420
when I saw the makeup job of his like flaky skin.
我真的被震惊到了。

448
00:19:23.420 --> 00:19:24.760
His face and his lips.
他的脸和嘴唇。

449
00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.640
His lips were so disturbing.
他的嘴唇太让人不安了。

450
00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:30.800
I think they used our real reaction because I remember it.
我想他们用了我们真实的反应，因为我记得那一幕。

451
00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:32.580
I remember being completely horrified.
我记得当时完全被吓坏了。

452
00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:33.460
I was like, oh my gosh.
我当时心想，天哪。

453
00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:34.780
Oh my God, Ed, what happened to you?
天哪，艾德，你这是怎么了？

454
00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:42.820
Well, let's get into the meat of this episode, or should I say the blubber of this episode.
好了，让我们进入本集的核心内容，或者我该说，本集的“肥肉”部分。

455
00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:46.400
David Wallace is going to call Dwight and tell him some news.
大卫·华莱士要给德怀特打电话，告诉他一个消息。

456
00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:47.040
Yeah.
没错。

457
00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:51.760
He's very excited, puts him on speakerphone only to want to take him off speakerphone because
他非常兴奋，开了免提，结果又想关掉免提，因为

458
00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:52.860
he doesn't want Jim to hear.
他不想让吉姆听到。

459
00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:59.080
Well, I mean, Jim rips the handheld part off the main phone and now he's got to be on speaker.
嗯，我的意思是，吉姆把电话听筒从座机上扯了下来，现在他只能用免提了。

460
00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:05.440
Yes, and what we learn is that the Scranton White Pages have dropped their paper supplier
是的，我们了解到斯克兰顿白页电话簿已经放弃了他们合作了

461
00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:08.240
of 10 years and they are up for grabs.
10年的纸张供应商，现在这个业务空出来了。

462
00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:12.660
And he wants Dwight and Jim to go and get this business.
他想让德怀特和吉姆去拿下这个业务。

463
00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:16.480
He says he wants the top salesman, which is Dwight.
他说他想要最好的销售员，也就是德怀特。

464
00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:17.120
Yeah.
没错。

465
00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:18.700
Dwight is over the moon.
德怀特高兴坏了。

466
00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:19.740
He's so excited.
他太兴奋了。

467
00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:20.520
So excited.
非常兴奋。

468
00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:24.780
He has a talking head where he says, the White Pages aren't something that you want or
他有一个访谈镜头，他说，白页电话簿不是你想要或

469
00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:29.660
need, but it shows up on your doorstep anyway, and there's a reason why it's called the White
需要的东西，但它还是会出现在你的家门口，这就是为什么它被称为“白

470
00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:30.140
Whale.
鲸”的原因。

471
00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:35.120
And then he flips through all the pages and he says, look at all that sweet blubber.
然后他翻阅了所有的页面说，看看那些甜美的肥肉。

472
00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:36.000
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

473
00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:38.260
Need a lot of paper to make the White Pages.
制作白页电话簿需要大量的纸张。

474
00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:38.840
This is a big score.
这是一笔大买卖。

475
00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:42.280
I think it might be time for a little mini, a mini dive.
我想现在是时候来个小小的，小小的深入挖掘了。

476
00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.340
On the White Pages?
关于白页电话簿？

477
00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:46.060
On the first ever phone book.
关于史上第一本电话簿。

478
00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:47.760
Oh, the first ever.
哦，史上第一本。

479
00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.100
I was so curious.
我太好奇了。

480
00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:51.400
I was like, you know, I love an origin story.
我心想，你知道的，我喜欢起源故事。

481
00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:51.900
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

482
00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:54.720
So here's a little bit about the first phone book ever.
所以这里有一些关于史上第一本电话簿的小知识。

483
00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:56.640
It all went down in Connecticut.
这一切都发生在康涅狄格州。

484
00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:57.540
Connecticut.
康涅狄格州。

485
00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:59.080
And he would be so proud.
他一定会感到非常自豪。

486
00:20:59.280 --> 00:20:59.560
Yeah.
没错。

487
00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:02.880
Here's what the UConn Library website had to share.
这是康涅狄格大学图书馆网站上的分享内容。

488
00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:08.640
George Coy was the manager of a telegraph office in New Haven, Connecticut, and he attended
乔治·科伊是康涅狄格州纽黑文市一家电报局的经理，他在1877年4月参加了

489
00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:14.900
a demonstration of the telephone by inventor Alexander Graham Bell in April 1877.
发明家亚历山大·格拉汉姆·贝尔的电话演示会。

490
00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:22.720
This led to Coy establishing the world's first public telephone exchange in January of 1878.
这促使科伊在1878年1月建立了世界上第一个公共电话交换局。

491
00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:30.740
Lady, it says he used carriage bolts, teapot lids, and wire to make a switchboard of eight lines.
天哪，上面说他用了马车螺栓、茶壶盖和电线做了一个八线交换机。

492
00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:33.940
I mean, this feels like a little MacGyver action.
我的意思是，这感觉有点像马盖先的作风。

493
00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:34.520
Yeah.
没错。

494
00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:35.040
Right?
对吧？

495
00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:38.240
It feels like something your kid does in science class.
感觉就像你孩子在科学课上做的事情。

496
00:21:38.240 --> 00:21:44.120
I know, but it worked, and the New Haven District Telephone Company was established, and it was
我知道，但它确实奏效了，纽黑文地区电话公司成立了，这是

497
00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:46.900
the first public telephone company in the world.
世界上第一家公共电话公司。

498
00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:47.760
Wow.
哇。

499
00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:50.540
The company established another firSt.
该公司还创造了另一个第一。

500
00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:53.280
It produced the first ever telephone directory.
它制作了史上第一本电话簿。

501
00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:57.640
The directory listed 50 customers with no phone numbers.
名录上列出了50位没有电话号码的客户。

502
00:21:57.980 --> 00:21:58.420
Oh.
哦。

503
00:21:58.700 --> 00:21:58.980
Yeah.
是啊。

504
00:21:59.140 --> 00:22:00.100
How do I call them?
那我该怎么给他们打电话呢？

505
00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:03.780
Well, to us now, this might seem odd, but back then...
嗯，对我们现在来说，这可能看起来很奇怪，但在当时……

506
00:22:03.780 --> 00:22:04.980
How many pages was this?
这本名录有多少页？

507
00:22:05.600 --> 00:22:08.340
It was, I mean, just three pages.
它，我是说，只有三页。

508
00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:09.660
It's like a little pamphlet.
就像一本小册子。

509
00:22:09.780 --> 00:22:10.700
I saw a picture of it.
我见过它的照片。

510
00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:10.900
Okay.
好的。

511
00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:12.020
Here's how it worked.
它是这样运作的。

512
00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:15.360
Since every call was connected manually, you know, by a...
因为每通电话都是人工接通的，你知道，通过……

513
00:22:15.360 --> 00:22:16.300
Oh, you didn't dial a number.
哦，你不用拨号码。

514
00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:16.740
No.
是的。

515
00:22:16.900 --> 00:22:22.280
You were connected by a central switchboard operator, and the subscriber list was so small,
你是通过中央总机接线员接通的，而且用户名单非常少，

516
00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:23.560
no numbers were necessary.
根本不需要号码。

517
00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:24.080
Sure.
确实。

518
00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:28.120
You would just dial up the person, the switchboard, and you'd be like...
你只需要呼叫对方，就是总机，然后你会说……

519
00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:29.160
Connect me to...
帮我接通……

520
00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:30.100
...to whoever.
……接通某某人。

521
00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:30.700
Right.
没错。

522
00:22:30.700 --> 00:22:34.260
Yeah, Angela Kinsey, if you were in the pamphlet, I'd know you have a phone.
是啊，安吉拉·金赛，如果你在小册子上，我就知道你有电话。

523
00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:34.820
That's right.
没错。

524
00:22:35.200 --> 00:22:35.500
Huh.
哈。

525
00:22:35.800 --> 00:22:41.220
What's amazing is this company grew and went through many different configurations, but
令人惊奇的是，这家公司不断发展，经历了许多不同的架构调整，但

526
00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:46.100
it provided independent telecommunication service to the state of Connecticut until 1998.
它一直为康涅狄格州提供独立的电信服务，直到1998年。

527
00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:47.160
Wow.
哇。

528
00:22:47.420 --> 00:22:47.960
I know.
我知道。

529
00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:52.380
I love reading about the origin of things, but it also reminded me of a simpler time.
我喜欢阅读关于事物起源的内容，但这同时也让我想起了那个更简单的时代。

530
00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:59.340
And when I moved to Archer City, Texas, I would ask for people's phone numbers, and
当我搬到德克萨斯州的阿彻城时，我会问别人的电话号码，然后

531
00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:00.700
they would just give you four digits.
他们只会给你四个数字。

532
00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:03.320
Because the first ones were all the same?
因为前面的号码都一样吗？

533
00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:03.960
Yes.
是的。

534
00:23:04.080 --> 00:23:05.300
And the town was so small.
而且那个镇子太小了。

535
00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:10.960
So I moved from Indonesia, you know, and then I moved to this small town, and I thought
所以我从印度尼西亚搬来，你知道，然后搬到了这个小镇，我以为

536
00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:12.200
everyone just had four numbers.
每个人只有四个数字。

537
00:23:12.760 --> 00:23:13.580
That's so funny.
太搞笑了。

538
00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:16.660
And when I went to college, I would be like, what are your four numbers?
当我上大学时，我会问，你的那四个数字是多少？

539
00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:18.580
I know.
我知道。

540
00:23:18.720 --> 00:23:20.020
It's just crazy to think about.
想起来真是太疯狂了。

541
00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:22.340
People were like, don't you need all of them, Ange?
人们会说，安吉，你不需要全部号码吗？

542
00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:23.520
I'm like, no, I just need four.
我说，不用，我只需要四个。

543
00:23:23.660 --> 00:23:24.140
And they're like, nope.
他们就说，不行。

544
00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:24.880
Just need the last four.
只需要最后四位。

545
00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:25.200
Nope.
不行。

546
00:23:25.560 --> 00:23:27.000
Do you remember 411?
你还记得411吗？

547
00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:28.020
Yes.
记得。

548
00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:29.340
Is that still a thing?
那现在还有吗？

549
00:23:29.940 --> 00:23:36.820
Like you used to call up 411 and be like, I'm looking for the phone number of something
就像你以前会打411，然后说，我在找某个东西的电话号码，

550
00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:38.600
like Lewis's tires.
比如刘易斯轮胎店。

551
00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:39.480
I don't know.
我不知道。

552
00:23:39.580 --> 00:23:40.260
Should we call it?
我们要打过去吗？

553
00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:41.100
Sure.
当然。

554
00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:41.920
I mean, I'm scared.
我是说，我很害怕。

555
00:23:42.300 --> 00:23:44.500
What happens when you dial 411 now?
现在拨打411会发生什么？

556
00:23:44.660 --> 00:23:45.300
Let's not be scared.
别害怕。

557
00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:45.540
Let's see.
我们来看看。

558
00:23:45.540 --> 00:23:46.640
Well, what are we going to ask for?
好吧，我们要问什么呢？

559
00:23:47.160 --> 00:23:48.720
Ask for Pizza Hut.
问问必胜客。

560
00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:49.120
Okay.
好的。

561
00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:55.510
The service you are calling is not available from this location.
您所拨打的服务在此地区无法使用。

562
00:23:55.670 --> 00:23:56.050
Oh.
噢。

563
00:23:56.090 --> 00:23:57.170
If this is an emergency.
如果是紧急情况。

564
00:23:57.490 --> 00:23:57.830
Oh.
噢。

565
00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:00.350
Well, we'll never get Pizza Hut now.
好吧，我们现在永远也吃不到必胜客了。

566
00:24:00.350 --> 00:24:00.790
Nope.
没错。

567
00:24:01.230 --> 00:24:03.330
I'm just going to go without pizza today, I guess.
我想我今天只能不吃披萨了。

568
00:24:03.590 --> 00:24:05.230
Now you have me hungry for pizza.
现在你让我馋披萨了。

569
00:24:05.410 --> 00:24:05.690
Sorry.
抱歉。

570
00:24:06.310 --> 00:24:07.270
Well, there you go.
好吧，就是这样。

571
00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:09.530
A little bit of the origin of the first phone book.
关于第一本电话簿起源的一点小知识。

572
00:24:09.690 --> 00:24:11.570
The first phone book would not have been a whale.
第一本电话簿肯定不是像鲸鱼那么大。

573
00:24:11.870 --> 00:24:14.230
It would have been like a little, like a minnow.
它应该像一条小鱼，像鲦鱼那样。

574
00:24:15.090 --> 00:24:15.470
Yes.
是的。

575
00:24:16.150 --> 00:24:21.510
Also during this phone call with David Wallace, Dwight asks if Tom Peterman is still in charge
同样在与大卫·华莱士的这通电话中，德怀特问汤姆·彼得曼是否还负责

576
00:24:21.510 --> 00:24:22.670
of the White Pages account.
白页电话簿的客户。

577
00:24:23.370 --> 00:24:24.770
We find out, no.
我们发现，并没有。

578
00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:28.650
It is now run by a woman, but David doesn't know her name.
现在由一位女士负责，但大卫不知道她的名字。

579
00:24:29.130 --> 00:24:30.750
Phyllis immediately perks up.
菲利斯立刻振作了起来。

580
00:24:30.870 --> 00:24:31.750
She's like, no, no, no.
她心想，不，不，不。

581
00:24:31.970 --> 00:24:33.610
Dwight cannot handle this sale.
德怀特搞不定这笔生意。

582
00:24:33.790 --> 00:24:35.190
He is horrible with women.
他很不擅长应付女性。

583
00:24:35.470 --> 00:24:35.850
Yes.
是的。

584
00:24:35.850 --> 00:24:37.990
He kept calling Gina Rogers Gina.
他一直管吉娜·罗杰斯叫吉娜。

585
00:24:38.430 --> 00:24:38.990
Yes.
是的。

586
00:24:39.270 --> 00:24:42.010
She said she had to correct him five times.
她说她不得不纠正他五次。

587
00:24:42.310 --> 00:24:43.930
Dwight says, Gina said that?
德怀特说，吉娜真这么说了？

588
00:24:44.230 --> 00:24:45.990
The scene was actually longer.
这一幕其实更长。

589
00:24:45.990 --> 00:24:51.490
And in the shooting draft, Dwight then turns to Angela and asks her, did I ever make you
在拍摄剧本中，德怀特随后转向安吉拉问她，我有没有让你

590
00:24:51.490 --> 00:24:52.070
feel uncomfortable?
感到不舒服？

591
00:24:52.570 --> 00:24:53.710
This is how it read.
剧本上是这么写的。

592
00:24:54.330 --> 00:24:55.530
Dwight, false.
德怀特：错误。

593
00:24:55.910 --> 00:24:59.610
Angela, did I make you uncomfortable when I'd have sex with you in the warehouse?
德怀特：安吉拉，当我在仓库里和你发生关系时，我让你感到不舒服了吗？

594
00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:01.590
Angela, quickly for camera.
安吉拉，对着镜头迅速回答。

595
00:25:01.910 --> 00:25:05.290
I was a virgin before marriage and I have never set foot in a warehouse.
我在婚前是处女，而且我从未踏进过仓库一步。

596
00:25:06.490 --> 00:25:11.690
So they let us do a bunch of takes and in one we improvised and it made it into deleted
所以他们让我们拍了很多条，其中一条我们即兴发挥了，后来被放进了删减

597
00:25:11.690 --> 00:25:12.150
scenes.
片段里。

598
00:25:12.370 --> 00:25:13.170
I want you to hear it.
我想让你们听听。

599
00:25:13.770 --> 00:25:15.710
Dwight, you make women feel uncomfortable.
德怀特，你让女性感到不舒服。

600
00:25:15.990 --> 00:25:17.170
That, ah, come on.
那个，啊，拜托。

601
00:25:17.370 --> 00:25:18.330
That is so not true.
那根本不是真的。

602
00:25:18.490 --> 00:25:23.710
Angela, when we would have meetings in the warehouse, did I make you feel uncomfortable?
安吉拉，以前我们在仓库开会的时候，我有让你感到不舒服吗？

603
00:25:24.550 --> 00:25:26.690
Uh, those meetings were very brief.
呃，那些会议都很简短。

604
00:25:27.930 --> 00:25:28.950
Boring, even.
甚至很无聊。

605
00:25:29.770 --> 00:25:31.210
I remember them being...
我记得它们是……

606
00:25:31.210 --> 00:25:32.030
Well, they weren't.
好吧，它们并不无聊。

607
00:25:33.390 --> 00:25:35.510
Oh, Angela, that is so funny.
噢，安吉拉，那太好笑了。

608
00:25:35.770 --> 00:25:36.170
I know.
我知道。

609
00:25:36.210 --> 00:25:37.410
That is such a good improv.
那段即兴表演太棒了。

610
00:25:37.430 --> 00:25:40.290
It was so fun when I was like, it was very brief.
我说“那很简短”的时候真的太好玩了。

611
00:25:41.330 --> 00:25:43.950
Rain's face as Dwight was like, hey.
雷恩演德怀特说“嘿”的时候，他的表情。

612
00:25:46.810 --> 00:25:49.590
Well, Phyllis is not going to let this go, you guys.
伙计们，菲利斯是不会善罢甘休的。

613
00:25:49.750 --> 00:25:55.370
She's like, listen, an account this size could double their gross, you know, their salaries,
她说，听着，这么大的一笔客户可以让他们的总收入翻倍，你知道，他们的薪水，

614
00:25:55.550 --> 00:25:56.050
their bonuses.
他们的奖金。

615
00:25:56.290 --> 00:25:57.890
Pizza Friday could come back.
周五披萨日可能又要回来了。

616
00:25:58.270 --> 00:26:00.390
They're not going to be able to call Pizza Hut, though.
不过他们没法打给必胜客了。

617
00:26:00.710 --> 00:26:01.770
Not with 411.
打114查号台可查不到。

618
00:26:01.970 --> 00:26:02.530
No, they're not.
不，他们查不到。

619
00:26:03.090 --> 00:26:05.250
Pam says, Jim, can you go instead?
帕姆说，吉姆，你能代替我去吗？

620
00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:06.610
But he can't.
但他去不了。

621
00:26:06.770 --> 00:26:11.470
He has his first board meeting conference call for his new business.
他要参加新公司的第一次董事会电话会议。

622
00:26:11.470 --> 00:26:11.910
Yeah.
是啊。

623
00:26:12.170 --> 00:26:12.570
Yeah.
是啊。

624
00:26:12.850 --> 00:26:14.610
So, he's busy.
所以，他很忙。

625
00:26:15.430 --> 00:26:17.210
Dwight's going to run point on this.
德怀特要负责这件事。

626
00:26:17.330 --> 00:26:17.830
Oh, no.
噢，不。

627
00:26:17.990 --> 00:26:18.590
Buckle in.
系好安全带吧。

628
00:26:19.570 --> 00:26:23.190
Meanwhile, we have this whole other storyline that really cracked me up.
与此同时，我们还有另一条让我笑喷了的故事线。

629
00:26:23.270 --> 00:26:24.170
We talked about it.
我们讨论过它。

630
00:26:24.730 --> 00:26:25.170
Movember.
