比如，为什么我需要细腰？

947
00:39:27.010 --> 00:39:34.110
And by the way, just full disclosure, this might be a question I'm asking because I don't have a waiSt.
顺便说一下，坦白讲，我问这个问题可能是因为我根本没有腰。

948
00:39:34.330 --> 00:39:38.890
I have a cylinder for a body of like a, just like a, what would you like?
我的身体就像个圆柱体，就像个，怎么说呢？

949
00:39:39.010 --> 00:39:39.730
Well, this is what happens.
嗯，事情就是这样。

950
00:39:39.730 --> 00:39:41.530
I don't go in at the waiSt.
我的腰部没有向内收。

951
00:39:41.550 --> 00:39:41.670
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

952
00:39:41.870 --> 00:39:43.310
Maybe I did when I was younger.
也许我年轻的时候有过。

953
00:39:43.310 --> 00:39:44.970
Yes, everyone does when they're younger.
是的，每个人年轻时都会这样。

954
00:39:45.230 --> 00:39:50.030
But do you remember, I mean, there's a point in your life where you go to your family reunion
但你还记得吗，我是说，在你生命中总有一个时刻，当你去参加家庭聚会时

955
00:39:50.030 --> 00:39:55.310
and you're in your 20s and you're looking out at your aunts and they're all talking by the food table
你二十多岁，看着你的阿姨们，她们都在餐桌旁聊天

956
00:39:55.310 --> 00:39:58.590
and they all look like marshmallows with like toothpick legs?
她们看起来都像长着牙签腿的棉花糖？

957
00:39:58.810 --> 00:39:59.230
Yeah.
是啊。

958
00:39:59.590 --> 00:40:01.030
That's the phase of life we're at.
这就是我们所处的人生阶段。

959
00:40:01.230 --> 00:40:02.830
We're marshmallows with toothpicks.
我们就是长着牙签腿的棉花糖。

960
00:40:03.110 --> 00:40:04.290
We've lost our waiSt.
我们已经没有腰了。

961
00:40:04.410 --> 00:40:04.970
It happens.
这很正常。

962
00:40:05.170 --> 00:40:06.070
It does happen.
确实如此。

963
00:40:06.210 --> 00:40:07.490
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

964
00:40:07.530 --> 00:40:11.310
The fashion, though, is still designed for the waiSt.
现在的时尚设计依然是针对有腰身的人。

965
00:40:11.530 --> 00:40:12.430
Not for the marshmallow.
而不是针对棉花糖身材。

966
00:40:12.650 --> 00:40:13.050
I know.
我知道。

967
00:40:13.110 --> 00:40:13.250
No.
不。

968
00:40:13.410 --> 00:40:13.550
I know.
我知道。

969
00:40:13.550 --> 00:40:17.210
And we need more fashion for the cylinder body.
我们需要更多适合圆柱形身材的时尚设计。

970
00:40:17.330 --> 00:40:17.710
Yes.
没错。

971
00:40:17.890 --> 00:40:18.230
You know?
你懂吗？

972
00:40:18.310 --> 00:40:19.350
Not for the hourglass.
不是为沙漏型身材设计的。

973
00:40:19.610 --> 00:40:22.110
No, for the straight, for the rectangle.
不，是为直筒型，为长方形身材设计的。

974
00:40:22.370 --> 00:40:23.450
I don't know what you call it.
我不知道你们管这叫什么。

975
00:40:23.490 --> 00:40:24.730
Yes, I call it a marshmallow.
是的，我管它叫棉花糖身材。

976
00:40:24.730 --> 00:40:27.410
But I go from my shoulder to my hips.
我的肩膀到臀部是一条线。

977
00:40:27.670 --> 00:40:29.490
It's just a straight line.
就是一条直线。

978
00:40:29.750 --> 00:40:29.930
Yes.
是的。

979
00:40:30.330 --> 00:40:30.770
Right.
没错。

980
00:40:31.030 --> 00:40:31.250
Yeah.
是啊。

981
00:40:31.430 --> 00:40:34.290
So it wouldn't matter if you put shoulder pads on me.
所以就算给我加垫肩也没用。

982
00:40:34.630 --> 00:40:35.630
No, it wouldn't.
不，没用的。

983
00:40:35.790 --> 00:40:36.610
It's not.
根本没用。

984
00:40:36.930 --> 00:40:38.690
There's still no waist happening.
还是没有腰。

985
00:40:38.950 --> 00:40:41.170
You'd have to put giant shoulder pads on me.
你得给我加巨大的垫肩才行。

986
00:40:41.270 --> 00:40:45.190
They never worked on me because shoulder pads are like one size fits all.
它们在我身上从来没起过作用，因为垫肩通常是均码的。

987
00:40:45.410 --> 00:40:46.110
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

988
00:40:46.250 --> 00:40:48.290
Not all shoulders are the same size.
并不是所有人的肩膀都一样宽。

989
00:40:48.710 --> 00:40:52.770
So you put a shoulder pad on me that you would put on someone taller.
所以如果你给我用那种给高个子准备的垫肩，

990
00:40:52.770 --> 00:40:54.650
And I lost my neck.
我的脖子就没了。

991
00:40:54.950 --> 00:40:58.570
It was like a little head sitting on these two little shelves.
看起来就像一个小脑袋架在两个小架子上。

992
00:40:58.790 --> 00:40:59.370
I don't know.
我不知道该怎么说。

993
00:40:59.510 --> 00:41:00.450
I look like a turtle.
我看起来像只乌龟。

994
00:41:00.710 --> 00:41:02.670
I just remember that movie Working Girl.
我只记得那部电影《上班女郎》了。

995
00:41:02.890 --> 00:41:03.210
Yes.
是的。

996
00:41:03.210 --> 00:41:05.190
There were so many shoulder pads in that movie.
那部电影里有太多的垫肩了。

997
00:41:05.330 --> 00:41:05.410
So many shoulder pads.
太多的垫肩。

998
00:41:05.730 --> 00:41:07.610
And I do remember Joan Crawford.
我还记得琼·克劳馥。

999
00:41:07.790 --> 00:41:12.790
When she walks into that boardroom of the Pepsi company and she goes, don't.
当她走进百事公司的董事会会议室，她说，别那样。

1000
00:41:15.420 --> 00:41:15.840
Ugh.
呃。

1001
00:41:16.220 --> 00:41:18.020
Now Joan Crawford could do a shoulder pad.
琼·克劳馥确实能驾驭垫肩装。

1002
00:41:18.020 --> 00:41:18.300
She could.
确实能。

1003
00:41:18.500 --> 00:41:19.280
She gets the pass.
她拿到了通行证。

1004
00:41:19.420 --> 00:41:20.440
She's the one.
非她莫属。

1005
00:41:20.440 --> 00:41:20.960
Yes.
没错。

1006
00:41:22.500 --> 00:41:23.320
There it is.
就是它了。

1007
00:41:23.440 --> 00:41:23.880
There it is.
就是它了。

1008
00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:25.120
I hope you liked it.
希望你们喜欢。

1009
00:41:25.280 --> 00:41:26.080
I liked it.
我很喜欢。

1010
00:41:26.200 --> 00:41:30.620
I have one background catch here in this scene at 11 minutes and 16 seconds.
这一幕在11分16秒处，我发现了一个背景细节。

1011
00:41:31.040 --> 00:41:35.800
Did anyone else watching this wonder what the heck Pam and Dwight are driving past?
还有谁在看的时候纳闷帕姆和德怀特开车经过的是什么吗？

1012
00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:38.740
It looks like a bunch of orange vehicles.
看起来像是一堆橙色的车。

1013
00:41:38.740 --> 00:41:44.340
Maybe like road crew vehicles, you know, or like some kind of transportation orange vehicles.
可能是道路施工车辆，你知道的，或者某种运输用的橙色车辆。

1014
00:41:44.340 --> 00:41:45.140
I didn't know this.
我之前不知道这个。

1015
00:41:45.140 --> 00:41:48.440
And then lots of stuff that looks like bagged up trash.
还有很多看起来像是一袋袋垃圾的东西。

1016
00:41:48.660 --> 00:41:52.040
Anyone else go to 11 minutes, 16 seconds and be like, what the heck is that?
还有谁去看了11分16秒，然后心想，那到底是什么鬼？

1017
00:41:52.160 --> 00:41:52.740
What was it?
那是什么？

1018
00:41:52.860 --> 00:41:53.580
I don't know.
我不知道。

1019
00:41:53.780 --> 00:41:54.100
Oh.
噢。

1020
00:41:54.300 --> 00:41:55.160
I took a screen grab.
我截了图。

1021
00:41:55.400 --> 00:41:56.200
We're questioning it.
我们提出了疑问。

1022
00:41:56.300 --> 00:41:57.320
We're not answering it.
但我们没给出答案。

1023
00:41:57.520 --> 00:41:58.640
Does anyone else know?
还有人知道吗？

1024
00:41:58.920 --> 00:41:59.640
Please write me.
请写信告诉我。

1025
00:41:59.860 --> 00:42:03.580
Well, we got another fan question about this scene from Gabriel M.
好吧，我们收到了另一位粉丝关于这一幕的提问，来自巴西的加布里埃尔·M。

1026
00:42:03.640 --> 00:42:05.180
in Brazil, who said,
他写道，

1027
00:42:05.300 --> 00:42:10.960
after four years, you guys might be able to finally end my seven-year-long queSt.
四年过去了，你们或许终于能终结我长达七年的追寻了。

1028
00:42:11.060 --> 00:42:14.800
There is a deleted scene where Pam and Dwight are in the car.
有一个删减片段是帕姆和德怀特在车里。

1029
00:42:15.140 --> 00:42:18.200
And Dwight is hyping himself up to some loud metal.
德怀特正在听着重金属音乐给自己打气。

1030
00:42:18.460 --> 00:42:21.480
Yes, he's hyping himself up to go win this big sale.
没错，他正在给自己打气，准备去拿下这笔大订单。

1031
00:42:21.720 --> 00:42:26.720
Yes, they're actually in the parking lot outside of the building where they're going to do this sale.
对，他们当时就在要去谈生意的办公楼外的停车场里。

1032
00:42:26.900 --> 00:42:29.080
He's doing that thing that he does, right?
他正在做他常做的那种动作，对吧？

1033
00:42:29.340 --> 00:42:36.660
So Gabriel goes on to say that after seeing Pam's discomfort to this metal music,
加布里埃尔接着说，在看到帕姆对这种金属乐感到不适后，

1034
00:42:36.920 --> 00:42:39.360
Dwight changes to a softer song.
德怀特换了一首柔和的歌。

1035
00:42:39.360 --> 00:42:39.760
Yeah.
没错。

1036
00:42:40.220 --> 00:42:45.100
Gabriel says, do you guys know either the song or the singer of the softer song?
加布里埃尔问，你们知道那首柔和的歌叫什么，或者歌手是谁吗？

1037
00:42:45.280 --> 00:42:49.100
I love that little snippet of it, but I've never been able to find it.
我很喜欢那小段音乐，但我一直没能找到它。

1038
00:42:49.480 --> 00:42:53.300
Well, I remember shooting this, but I couldn't remember the songs.
嗯，我记得拍过这场戏，但我记不起那两首歌了。

1039
00:42:53.540 --> 00:42:55.920
And I didn't recognize it when I rewatched it.
重看的时候我也没认出来。

1040
00:42:56.080 --> 00:43:03.760
That's because Steve Burgess told me that it was scripted to switch from a Metallica track
那是因为史蒂夫·伯吉斯告诉我，剧本里写的是从一首金属乐队的歌

1041
00:43:03.760 --> 00:43:05.800
to a Carpenter's track.
切换到一首卡朋特乐队的歌。

1042
00:43:06.120 --> 00:43:06.240
Okay.
好吧。

1043
00:43:07.140 --> 00:43:08.420
Metallica said yes.
金属乐队同意了。

1044
00:43:08.680 --> 00:43:09.080
Great.
太棒了。

1045
00:43:09.300 --> 00:43:10.480
The Carpenter said no.
但卡朋特乐队拒绝了。

1046
00:43:11.000 --> 00:43:12.180
So then what did we switch to?
那后来我们换成了什么？

1047
00:43:12.380 --> 00:43:14.880
We ended up recording it with no music.
我们最后录制的时候其实没有音乐。

1048
00:43:15.100 --> 00:43:17.340
And this is why I couldn't remember.
这就是我记不起来的原因。

1049
00:43:17.620 --> 00:43:23.180
We added the music in post, and we just used what Steve called library tracks.
我们在后期制作时才加上了音乐，用的就是史蒂夫所说的“素材库音乐”。

1050
00:43:23.480 --> 00:43:27.520
It's just generic tracks of styles of music.
就是那种风格通用的背景音乐。

1051
00:43:27.520 --> 00:43:29.360
It's much less expensive.
这便宜多了。

1052
00:43:29.720 --> 00:43:32.600
But Steve said, unfortunately, he didn't have any information about it,
但史蒂夫说，很遗憾，他对此一无所知，

1053
00:43:32.680 --> 00:43:35.360
but it's kind of like the stock photo of the music world.
但这就像音乐界的库存照片一样。

1054
00:43:35.600 --> 00:43:39.400
So they were not like songs that we could point to.
所以它们并不是我们能指名道姓的歌曲。

1055
00:43:39.580 --> 00:43:41.900
They were just this stock music.
它们只是那种库存音乐。

1056
00:43:42.300 --> 00:43:43.860
That's why I couldn't figure it out.
这就是我为什么搞不清楚的原因。

1057
00:43:44.000 --> 00:43:44.320
Yes.
是的。

1058
00:43:44.500 --> 00:43:46.700
And also, Gabriel, why you couldn't figure it out.
也是加布里埃尔你搞不清楚的原因。

1059
00:43:46.840 --> 00:43:47.160
Right.
没错。

1060
00:43:47.660 --> 00:43:50.360
Well, Angela and Oscar are now at the yoga studio.
好了，安吉拉和奥斯卡现在在瑜伽馆。

1061
00:43:50.800 --> 00:43:56.760
They're actually in a food court where they can look through like a glass window into the yoga studio.
他们其实是在美食广场，透过玻璃窗看着瑜伽馆里。

1062
00:43:56.760 --> 00:44:00.380
Yeah, you guys are drinking – are you drinking shakes?
是啊，你们在喝——你们是在喝奶昔吗？

1063
00:44:00.660 --> 00:44:01.920
Are you drinking smoothies?
你们是在喝果昔吗？

1064
00:44:02.220 --> 00:44:03.600
They were like smoothies.
看起来像是果昔。

1065
00:44:03.660 --> 00:44:03.880
Okay.
好吧。

1066
00:44:04.160 --> 00:44:07.540
The senator walks in with a very petite blonde.
参议员带着一个非常娇小的金发女郎走了进来。

1067
00:44:07.540 --> 00:44:10.880
This really, really sends Angela off the deep thing.
这真的让安吉拉彻底抓狂了。

1068
00:44:10.880 --> 00:44:13.080
Oh, she's a double zero for sure, for sure.
噢，她绝对是00码身材，肯定的。

1069
00:44:13.260 --> 00:44:16.920
And then she starts adjusting his hips for downward dog.
然后她开始帮他调整下犬式的臀部姿势。

1070
00:44:17.060 --> 00:44:18.800
Angela's like, I have heard of this.
安吉拉心想，我听说过这个。

1071
00:44:18.880 --> 00:44:19.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1072
00:44:19.380 --> 00:44:20.000
Dog style.
狗爬式。

1073
00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:26.180
But then a guy walks up with a ponytail and gives the yoga instructor a big hug,
但随后一个扎马尾辫的男人走过来，给了瑜伽教练一个大大的拥抱，

1074
00:44:26.180 --> 00:44:27.560
and Angela is so relieved.
安吉拉如释重负。

1075
00:44:27.700 --> 00:44:29.320
She's like, ugh, guy with a ponytail.
她心想，呼，是个扎马尾辫的男人。

1076
00:44:29.480 --> 00:44:31.200
I'd like to see that run for office.
我倒想看看这种人怎么竞选公职。

1077
00:44:31.480 --> 00:44:32.000
Yes.
没错。

1078
00:44:32.140 --> 00:44:35.860
But then Oscar sees the senator hugging a man.
但接着奥斯卡看到参议员在拥抱一个男人。

1079
00:44:36.020 --> 00:44:36.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1080
00:44:36.680 --> 00:44:40.920
Who then starts giving him some adjustments as he's doing his yoga pose.
那个人随后开始在他做瑜伽姿势时帮他做调整。

1081
00:44:41.080 --> 00:44:41.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1082
00:44:41.260 --> 00:44:46.440
He says, Angela's ready to leave, but Oscar says, no, shut up.
他说安吉拉准备走了，但奥斯卡说，不，闭嘴。

1083
00:44:46.600 --> 00:44:47.040
We're staying.
我们要留下来。

1084
00:44:47.380 --> 00:44:48.760
The plot thickens.
剧情变得复杂了。

1085
00:44:49.260 --> 00:44:49.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1086
00:44:50.100 --> 00:44:54.100
Jim is still trying to take this phone call and make this meeting happen.
吉姆还在试图打这个电话并促成这次会议。

1087
00:44:54.380 --> 00:44:59.560
He now goes outside, but there's construction going on, and then he kind of leans on Meredith's
他现在走到外面，但那里正在施工，然后他靠在了梅雷迪思的

1088
00:44:59.560 --> 00:45:01.180
van and sets an alarm off.
货车上，触发了警报。

1089
00:45:01.540 --> 00:45:04.680
And this is my favorite line of the whole episode.
这是整集里我最喜欢的一句台词。

1090
00:45:04.900 --> 00:45:07.640
Hank comes out and is like, are those skateboarders back?
汉克走出来说，是不是那些玩滑板的又回来了？

1091
00:45:07.640 --> 00:45:10.700
And then Meredith is like, who was messing with my van?
然后梅雷迪思说，谁在动我的车？

1092
00:45:10.940 --> 00:45:15.820
And then Hank yells, and this is my favorite line, this ends now.
接着汉克大喊——这是我最喜欢的一句——到此为止了。

1093
00:45:16.540 --> 00:45:17.800
Like, he is done.
他真的是受够了。

1094
00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:21.640
He is ready to take on this whole pack of skateboarders.
他准备好要对付这整群玩滑板的人了。

1095
00:45:21.900 --> 00:45:25.660
And poor Jim is like, where can I talk to these people?
而可怜的吉姆心想，我到底能在哪里跟这些人谈话？

1096
00:45:26.200 --> 00:45:28.360
Oh, where can you talk to these people, Jim?
噢，吉姆，你能在哪里跟这些人谈话呢？

1097
00:45:28.520 --> 00:45:31.160
We've got a fan mail flurry to answer that question.
我们收到了一大堆粉丝来信来回答这个问题。

1098
00:45:31.380 --> 00:45:32.080
What is it?
是什么问题？

1099
00:45:32.180 --> 00:45:34.260
It really teed some people off.
这真的让一些人火冒三丈。

1100
00:45:34.260 --> 00:45:36.480
Fan question from Deanna H.
来自迪安娜·H的粉丝提问。

1101
00:45:36.540 --> 00:45:40.340
in Plant City, Florida, who said, why wouldn't Jim just go
在佛罗里达州普兰特城，有人问，吉姆为什么不直接去

1102
00:45:40.340 --> 00:45:42.280
into Andy's office to make the call?
安迪的办公室打那个电话呢？

1103
00:45:42.660 --> 00:45:43.800
Andy isn't there.
安迪不在那儿。

1104
00:45:44.640 --> 00:45:45.240
Sarah C.
来自新泽西州的莎拉·C.

1105
00:45:45.420 --> 00:45:49.760
from New Jersey said, I have been waiting so long to comment on Jim's phone
说，我等了这么久，就是为了评论吉姆的那个电话

1106
00:45:49.760 --> 00:45:50.020
call.
通话。

1107
00:45:50.140 --> 00:45:55.220
I was so frustrated with Jim in this episode because there was no need for this, Jim.
这一集里吉姆的表现让我太抓狂了，因为根本没必要这样，吉姆。

1108
00:45:55.660 --> 00:45:59.880
Here is a list of 10 places where Jim could have taken that call.
这里有一份清单，列出了吉姆本可以去接那个电话的10个地方。

1109
00:45:59.880 --> 00:46:03.840
I can't wait to hear this because one place came to mind immediately for me.
我迫不及待想听听了，因为我脑子里立刻就蹦出了一个地方。

1110
00:46:03.960 --> 00:46:05.140
I bet you can guess it.
我敢打赌你能猜到。

1111
00:46:05.260 --> 00:46:05.860
I don't know.
我不知道。

1112
00:46:06.040 --> 00:46:07.780
It's where all the secret stuff happens.
就是所有秘密发生的地方。

1113
00:46:07.980 --> 00:46:09.020
The secret stairwell.
秘密楼梯间。

1114
00:46:09.080 --> 00:46:09.780
The stairwell.
楼梯间。

1115
00:46:09.900 --> 00:46:11.740
Why didn't he go to the stairwell?
他为什么不去楼梯间呢？

1116
00:46:11.920 --> 00:46:14.060
Yes, that was number four on her liSt.
没错，那是她清单上的第四名。

1117
00:46:14.240 --> 00:46:15.080
Let's hear the reSt.
让我们听听剩下的。

1118
00:46:15.320 --> 00:46:15.680
All right.
好的。

1119
00:46:15.840 --> 00:46:17.720
Number one, Andy's office.
第一名，安迪的办公室。

1120
00:46:18.140 --> 00:46:20.240
Number two, Daryl's office.
第二名，达里尔的办公室。

1121
00:46:20.820 --> 00:46:23.280
Surely Daryl would have given him his office for this.
达里尔肯定会为了这事把办公室借给他的。

1122
00:46:23.400 --> 00:46:24.960
I mean, how long is this phone call going to be?
我是说，这通电话能打多久？

1123
00:46:25.100 --> 00:46:25.540
Not long.
不会太久。

1124
00:46:26.960 --> 00:46:29.040
Three, inside Pam and Jim's car.
第三，帕姆和吉姆的车里。

1125
00:46:29.740 --> 00:46:30.960
Yeah, I thought of that, too.
是啊，我也想到了这一点。

1126
00:46:31.520 --> 00:46:32.240
The stairwell.
楼梯间。

1127
00:46:32.480 --> 00:46:32.800
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1128
00:46:33.160 --> 00:46:38.180
Number five, close off the break room like how Toby did when he was having a counseling session
第五名，像托比和迈克尔进行心理咨询时那样，把休息室关上。

1129
00:46:38.180 --> 00:46:38.800
with Michael.
迈克尔。

1130
00:46:39.700 --> 00:46:43.040
Six, the former Michael Scott Paper Company room.
第六名，以前迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司的那个房间。

1131
00:46:43.240 --> 00:46:44.300
There it is.
就是那儿。

1132
00:46:44.620 --> 00:46:48.240
Seven, the room that they used for spying on Danny Cordray.
第七名，他们用来监视丹尼·科德雷的那个房间。

1133
00:46:49.020 --> 00:46:52.420
Number eight, the Dwight Schrute gym for muscles.
第八名，德怀特·舒鲁特的肌肉健身房。

1134
00:46:53.300 --> 00:46:55.940
Number nine, Ryan's closet.
第九名，瑞安的储物间。

1135
00:46:56.620 --> 00:46:57.360
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1136
00:46:57.360 --> 00:47:02.540
Number 10, the closet in your accounting where Jim and Pam sneak off in the episode PDA.
第十名，你们会计部那个储物间，吉姆和帕姆在《PDA》那一集里偷偷溜进去过。

1137
00:47:03.840 --> 00:47:05.400
This is a really good liSt.
这份清单真的很棒。

1138
00:47:06.200 --> 00:47:07.200
Really good liSt.
真的很棒。

1139
00:47:07.360 --> 00:47:08.720
I understand the whole liSt.
这份清单我全都理解。

1140
00:47:08.900 --> 00:47:12.400
The only two that I think would be difficult are Andy's office and Daryl's office.
我觉得只有安迪的办公室和达里尔的办公室比较难办。

1141
00:47:12.400 --> 00:47:13.180
I'll tell you why.
我告诉你为什么。

1142
00:47:13.340 --> 00:47:13.600
Why?
为什么？

1143
00:47:13.780 --> 00:47:17.200
Because people can look in and be nosy and be like, hey, what are you doing in here?
因为人们会往里看，还会多管闲事，问你在里面干什么。

1144
00:47:17.320 --> 00:47:18.420
Like, Kevin would be like, what's up?
比如凯文会问，怎么了？

1145
00:47:18.480 --> 00:47:19.380
What are we doing in here?
我们在里面干什么呢？

1146
00:47:19.440 --> 00:47:20.020
Are we hanging out?
我们在闲逛吗？

1147
00:47:20.320 --> 00:47:20.500
Yeah.
没错。

1148
00:47:20.840 --> 00:47:22.380
All the rest, I think, makes sense.
剩下的那些，我觉得都说得通。

1149
00:47:22.520 --> 00:47:23.560
I've got another one.
我还有一个。

1150
00:47:24.020 --> 00:47:24.420
Home.
家里。

1151
00:47:24.660 --> 00:47:25.000
Home.
回家。

1152
00:47:25.140 --> 00:47:25.660
Go home.
回家吧。

1153
00:47:26.020 --> 00:47:28.620
Who's in the office that's going to give you grief about it?
办公室里有谁会因为这事找你麻烦吗？

1154
00:47:28.740 --> 00:47:30.480
Dwight has left and Andy's not there.
德怀特走了，安迪也不在。

1155
00:47:31.300 --> 00:47:34.120
Toby is completely distracted by his Movember gang.
托比正忙着应付他的“胡子月”小团体，根本没空管你。

1156
00:47:34.300 --> 00:47:36.420
Just sneak out and go home and take the call.
偷偷溜走回家接电话就行了。

1157
00:47:36.640 --> 00:47:36.760
Go home.
回家吧。

1158
00:47:36.940 --> 00:47:38.100
They don't live that far.
他们住得又不远。

1159
00:47:38.440 --> 00:47:38.540
No.
不。

1160
00:47:39.140 --> 00:47:44.600
Dwight and Pam are now walking into the office where they're going to meet this new prospective client.
德怀特和帕姆现在走进办公室，准备去见那位潜在的新客户。

1161
00:47:45.300 --> 00:47:50.800
And Pam asks the receptionist, Molly, for the woman's name, but Molly won't tell her the name.
帕姆问前台莫莉那个女人的名字，但莫莉不肯告诉她。

1162
00:47:51.420 --> 00:47:53.460
And Pam starts to look around the room.
于是帕姆开始环顾四周。

1163
00:47:53.600 --> 00:47:59.140
And, Jen, I thought your performance was so great as you start to see multiple clues that this is Jan.
简，我觉得你当时的表演太棒了，因为你开始发现种种线索，意识到那个人就是简。

1164
00:47:59.940 --> 00:48:00.420
Yes.
是的。

1165
00:48:00.980 --> 00:48:06.140
You know, I asked Carrie about her role as Molly because she's so funny.
我问过凯莉关于她饰演莫莉的事，因为她演得太搞笑了。

1166
00:48:06.400 --> 00:48:09.980
I remember she did it at the table read, which often happened.
我记得她在剧本围读会上就演过，这种情况很常见。

1167
00:48:10.220 --> 00:48:14.960
Like, writers would read some of the smaller roles because sometimes those roles would get cut after the table read.
比如，编剧们会读一些小角色，因为有时这些角色在围读后会被删掉。

1168
00:48:15.100 --> 00:48:18.180
So they didn't want to cast them until they were, like, locked in.
所以他们不想在角色定下来之前就找演员。

1169
00:48:18.180 --> 00:48:18.620
Yes.
是的。

1170
00:48:19.340 --> 00:48:23.740
So she said that after the table read, they asked her to play the part.
她说围读会结束后，他们就邀请她来演这个角色。

1171
00:48:24.180 --> 00:48:29.860
And she said she had used to act in musicals in high schools and college but had never done any on-camera work before.
她说她高中和大学时演过音乐剧，但以前从没拍过影视剧。

1172
00:48:30.080 --> 00:48:35.200
And she said one of the things that she remembered the most from the shoot, it's a very funny story.
她说她对拍摄印象最深的一件事，是个非常有趣的故事。

1173
00:48:35.420 --> 00:48:39.420
She said she remembered walking on set and that I looked at her and I said,
她说记得自己走进片场时，我看着她说：

1174
00:48:39.580 --> 00:48:43.720
Oh, my gosh, I think you're wearing one of your sister's outfits.
“天哪，我觉得你穿的是我妹妹的衣服。”

1175
00:48:44.120 --> 00:48:45.180
One of Erin's outfits?
艾琳的衣服？

1176
00:48:45.460 --> 00:48:45.760
Yes.
是的。

1177
00:48:46.220 --> 00:48:47.920
Because, you know, that would happen sometimes.
因为你知道，这种事有时会发生。

1178
00:48:47.920 --> 00:48:53.160
We would have guest actors and I would look over and they would be wearing some of Pam's clothes.
我们会有客串演员，我转头一看，发现她们穿着帕姆的衣服。

1179
00:48:53.420 --> 00:48:53.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1180
00:48:53.720 --> 00:48:54.340
This happened.
确实发生过。

1181
00:48:54.540 --> 00:48:57.020
I'd be like, I think that's my jacket.
我会说：我觉得那是我的夹克。

1182
00:48:57.380 --> 00:48:57.560
Yeah.
没错。

1183
00:48:57.840 --> 00:49:03.500
And so, yes, it turns out if you look at this outfit, it is one of Erin's outfits.
所以，没错，如果你仔细看这套衣服，它确实是艾琳的衣服。

1184
00:49:03.560 --> 00:49:08.580
She was wearing an Erin outfit, which I actually think is a really sweet nod to them being sisters.
她穿着艾琳的衣服，我觉得这其实是对她们姐妹关系的一个非常温馨的暗示。

1185
00:49:08.880 --> 00:49:09.720
Yeah, I do too.
我也这么觉得。

1186
00:49:10.060 --> 00:49:13.880
Well, Jan is not happy that it is Dwight and Pam.
简对来的是德怀特和帕姆感到很不高兴。

1187
00:49:13.880 --> 00:49:18.380
She was really hoping for a reunion, a revenge union with David Wallace.
她本来真心希望能和戴维·华莱士重聚，进行一场复仇式的重逢。

1188
00:49:18.960 --> 00:49:24.720
Dwight is going to try to butter her up by complimenting Astrid, saying she could be a bubble bath model.
德怀特试图通过夸奖阿斯特丽德来讨好她，说她可以当泡泡浴模特。

1189
00:49:24.860 --> 00:49:26.420
So creepy, Dwight.
太恶心了，德怀特。

1190
00:49:26.420 --> 00:49:30.460
Melora does something in this scene that I had to go back.
梅洛拉在这场戏里做了一个动作，我不得不倒回去看。

1191
00:49:30.600 --> 00:49:32.480
I had to rewind because I thought it was so great.
我倒回去看了，因为我觉得那太棒了。

1192
00:49:32.620 --> 00:49:33.680
It's not in the script.
剧本里没有这一段。

1193
00:49:33.960 --> 00:49:37.220
It's just Melora being Jan and she's so brilliant.
那是梅洛拉完全进入了简的状态，她真是太天才了。

1194
00:49:37.640 --> 00:49:44.220
While she's frustrated and talking to them, Jan picks up a frame and wipes the dust off with her boob.
当她感到沮丧并与他们交谈时，简拿起一个相框，用胸部擦去了上面的灰尘。

1195
00:49:44.220 --> 00:49:45.000
I noticed that.
我注意到了。

1196
00:49:45.000 --> 00:49:45.660
On her shirt.
用她的衬衫。

1197
00:49:45.980 --> 00:49:46.460
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

1198
00:49:46.660 --> 00:49:48.020
That is not in the script.
剧本里根本没写。

1199
00:49:48.540 --> 00:49:49.720
Melora is so good.
梅洛拉演得太好了。

1200
00:49:49.960 --> 00:49:51.120
We got a lot of fan mail.
我们收到了很多粉丝来信。

1201
00:49:51.260 --> 00:49:54.240
People wanted to know whose idea it was to bring Melora back.
大家想知道是谁提议让梅洛拉回归的。

1202
00:49:54.740 --> 00:49:56.400
Well, it was Greg.
嗯，是格雷格。

1203
00:49:56.900 --> 00:50:01.800
In this final season, he wanted us to touch base with some of the office favorites.
在这一最终季里，他希望我们能让办公室里的一些人气角色回归。

1204
00:50:02.000 --> 00:50:04.340
Remember, David Denman came back for Roy's wedding.
记得吗，大卫·丹曼之前就回来客串了罗伊的婚礼。

1205
00:50:04.480 --> 00:50:06.800
So this was the Jan episode.
所以这一集就是简的回归集。

1206
00:50:07.320 --> 00:50:12.860
And I traded texts with Melora because after I watched this episode, I was just like, God, she's so good.
我和梅洛拉互发了短信，因为看完这一集后，我心想，天哪，她演得太好了。

1207
00:50:13.120 --> 00:50:13.660
She's so good.
她真的太棒了。

1208
00:50:13.860 --> 00:50:17.200
She said it was so great to get to come back and see everybody.
她说能回来见到大家真是太好了。

1209
00:50:17.500 --> 00:50:21.760
She said she especially loved all of the Pam and Jan awkward interactions.
她说她特别喜欢帕姆和简之间所有那些尴尬的互动。

1210
00:50:22.420 --> 00:50:25.040
And I had to ask her about that skydiving photo.
我不得不问她关于那张跳伞照片的事。

1211
00:50:25.860 --> 00:50:27.140
I was like, did you?
我当时问，那是真的吗？

1212
00:50:27.340 --> 00:50:28.180
What is that?
那到底是什么？

1213
00:50:28.360 --> 00:50:30.080
Like, well, how did you do that?
就是，你们是怎么拍出来的？

1214
00:50:30.240 --> 00:50:34.060
Because it was scripted that there was going to be the skydiving photo in the office.
因为剧本里写了办公室里要出现那张跳伞照片。

1215
00:50:34.360 --> 00:50:34.680
And it's really big.
而且照片非常大。

1216
00:50:34.900 --> 00:50:35.920
It takes up the whole wall.
占据了整面墙。

1217
00:50:35.920 --> 00:50:42.900
She said that she had to come in one day and they put her in a skydiving suit and they had her lay on a table that was green.
她说她有一天专门去了一趟，他们让她穿上跳伞服，躺在一张绿色的桌子上。

1218
00:50:43.260 --> 00:50:46.420
And then they set up a fan and they blew it in her face.
然后他们架起一台风扇，对着她的脸吹。

1219
00:50:46.600 --> 00:50:50.840
And then in post, they removed the table and they put in the sky background.
后期制作时，他们去掉了桌子，换上了天空背景。

1220
00:50:51.140 --> 00:50:52.700
And that's how they got that picture.
那张照片就是这么拍出来的。

1221
00:50:53.340 --> 00:50:56.520
By the way, Angela, I don't know if you know this.
顺便问一下，安吉拉，不知道你知不知道。

1222
00:50:56.680 --> 00:50:59.500
There is a huge Monk crossover with Melora.
梅洛拉在《神探阿蒙》里有个重大的联动角色。

1223
00:51:00.820 --> 00:51:02.800
Yes, I have been told this.
是的，有人跟我提过。

1224
00:51:02.960 --> 00:51:05.160
She plays Trudy Monk.
她饰演特鲁迪·阿蒙。

1225
00:51:05.240 --> 00:51:05.600
Yes.
没错。

1226
00:51:05.920 --> 00:51:09.660
She is his ex-wife who was killed in a car bomb.
她是阿蒙的亡妻，死于汽车炸弹袭击。

1227
00:51:09.780 --> 00:51:12.380
And she comes back like as an apparition sometimes.
她有时会以幻影的形式出现。

1228
00:51:12.620 --> 00:51:13.060
Yes.
是的。

1229
00:51:13.280 --> 00:51:17.200
And her murder is the only one that Adrian Monk has not been able to solve.
她的谋杀案是阿蒙唯一没能侦破的案件。

1230
00:51:17.420 --> 00:51:20.040
It was like this whole runner of the series.
这几乎贯穿了整个剧集。

1231
00:51:20.660 --> 00:51:24.760
I'll have you know, she is back for the Monk movie, Monk's Last Case.
告诉你吧，她回归了《神探阿蒙》的电影版《阿蒙的最后案件》。

1232
00:51:25.000 --> 00:51:25.400
Oh.
哦。

1233
00:51:25.400 --> 00:51:27.960
I am not because my character went to jail.
我没能回归，因为我的角色坐牢了。

1234
00:51:27.960 --> 00:51:29.400
Sorry for the spoiler.
抱歉剧透了。

1235
00:51:30.260 --> 00:51:30.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1236
00:51:30.920 --> 00:51:34.360
Well, I loved all the little accents on Jan's desk.
我特别喜欢简办公桌上那些小装饰。

1237
00:51:34.360 --> 00:51:36.320
I'm sure a lot of you noticed these as well.
我相信你们很多人也注意到了。

1238
00:51:36.680 --> 00:51:38.880
She has her serenity candle.
她有她的“宁静”蜡烛。

1239
00:51:39.000 --> 00:51:41.120
She has a fancy pin set.
她有一套精致的别针。

1240
00:51:41.120 --> 00:51:43.040
She has clacky balls.
她有牛顿摆球。

1241
00:51:43.480 --> 00:51:44.520
Clacky balls.
牛顿摆球。

1242
00:51:44.640 --> 00:51:45.060
Yes.
对。

1243
00:51:45.060 --> 00:51:46.400
Oh, you know what?
哦，你知道吗？

1244
00:51:46.660 --> 00:51:48.260
My clacky balls are tangled.
我的牛顿摆球缠在一起了。

1245
00:51:48.740 --> 00:51:49.080
Oh.
哦。

1246
00:51:49.240 --> 00:51:50.540
You have to bring them in for Cassie.
你得带过来让凯西看看。

1247
00:51:50.560 --> 00:51:52.760
We need Cassie to untangle my clacky balls.
我们需要凯西来帮我解开我的牛顿摆球。

1248
00:51:53.560 --> 00:51:56.280
Jan not only has clacky balls, but she has a basket of balls.
简不仅有牛顿摆球，还有一个球筐。

1249
00:51:56.600 --> 00:52:00.120
And then she has one of those little mini zen, like, sand gardens.
然后她还有一个那种迷你的禅意沙盘。

1250
00:52:00.680 --> 00:52:05.460
And I just love the physical comedy callback that when Jan got stressed, she lit one of
我特别喜欢那个肢体喜剧的呼应，当简感到压力时，她会点燃其中一个

1251
00:52:05.460 --> 00:52:06.560
her own candles and started.
她自己的蜡烛，然后就开始了。

1252
00:52:06.840 --> 00:52:07.340
She wafts it.
她扇了扇。

1253
00:52:07.360 --> 00:52:07.760
Wafts it.
扇了扇。

1254
00:52:07.860 --> 00:52:08.200
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1255
00:52:08.500 --> 00:52:09.420
I love that, too.
我也很喜欢那个。

1256
